    "protein_name": "Oligopeptide-binding protein OppA",
    "ec": [],
    "function": "Part of the ABC transporter complex OppABCD involved in the uptake of oligopeptides. Peptide-binding protein that shows broad specificity but a moderate preference for hydrophobic oligopeptides and those that are 6-16 amino acids long. Can bind the tripeptide glutathione (GSH) and the nonapeptide bradykinin. Glutathione (GSH) uptake by mycobacteria through the OppABCD system contributes to the depletion of the GSH pool in infected macrophages, which impairs the ability of the macrophage to detoxify methylglyoxal (MG) and contributes to enhanced production of inflammatory cytokines. May also pr",
